format session-log-v1
stamp 20260824.043930
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The rule written as arithmetic, and the citation that named nothing
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, send each finished increment
think Opened the lap by running the roster COLD before touching anything. 38 of 38 green, so nothing preempted. The staged tree held the prior lap's whole round -- 32 files, REDS %178 and %179, the dated_spelling guard -- committed and never shipped. Shipped it first as its own signed round to origin and xykj61, since a finished increment sitting in the index is progress nobody can follow.
think Commit count 3359 after that push, so the council rota reads row 3359 mod 5 = 4 -- Earth and Mercury, the concrete. Read the one-clock naming law, TWO_ROOMS, and the marked value. The naming law is the one that bore: a stamp is unique across the whole tree forever, and every tool that reads one has to agree on its shape.
think Went looking in session-logs for the next crux and read the fold core on the way. `day_from_log_fname` in tools/rye/session_logs_archive.rye reads `if (fname[15] != '_') return null;` -- the narrow rule REDS %175 and %178 widened at nineteen other sites, written here as a byte comparison rather than as a regex.
obs The new dated_spelling guard scans .rye and passed truthfully over this file. It greps for regex SPELLINGS of the dated pattern, and there is no regex here to find. A guard that reads spellings sees only the places where the rule is spelled; a rule expressed as control flow is invisible to it, and the invisibility reads exactly like coverage.
obs Measured before repairing: zero files in any of the six enforced rooms stand flat by the narrow rule -- all 237 sprigless logs folded before the strictness landed. So this is prevention rather than repair, and the round says so rather than claiming a rescue.
think The meter for a rule's second form is a behavior test on metal, not a wider grep. Put the proof in the selftest the witness already runs: a sprigless .bron that must fold with its link repointed, and a day-only name that must stay exactly where it stands. One preview count of three proves the acceptance and the refusal together.
think Proved it from both sides -- restored the narrow line, watched the witness fail, restored the fix, watched it pass. A refusal proven only in the passing direction cannot be told from a bypass.
think Staged the round and ran the roster again, and this time one guard answered red: dated_path, refs_lost=188 against a ceiling of 187. The two new lost references were mine -- a full-digit `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.bron` and a `YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.kyri`, plausible sprigless names I reached for in a unit case and a ledger row, neither of them a file in this tree. This line writes them as placeholders on purpose; spelling the digits out here would make the citations a third time.
obs The mark law wrote this exact warning one lap ago -- illustrate with placeholders, cite only what exists -- and naming the fault did not prevent me repeating it. The meter did. That is REDS %181, and the transferable form is that an example is either a placeholder with letters where the digits go, or a real path, never a realistic-looking third thing -- inside a test string as much as in prose, since none of the three is invisible to a grep.
obs Found the two lines by diffing the scan's `list` output against a stashed tree rather than by rereading my own diff. A census that names every broken reference makes the question mechanical.
loom roster=standing_equipment guards=38 green=38 red=0 cold=true
loom roster=standing_equipment guards=38 green=37 red=1 after_git_add=true guard=dated_path refs_lost=188 ceiling=187
loom census=dated_path refs_lost=187 ceiling=187 under_ceiling=yes after_repair=true
file tools/rye/session_logs_archive.rye character 15 accepts the extension dot as well as the sprig underscore; three Zig unit cases added, two accepting a sprigless stamp and one refusing a countdown-prefix name
file tools/fixtures/session_logs_archive/20260703-120000.bron new -- a prior-day log carrying no sprig, which must fold
file tools/fixtures/session_logs_archive/20260814-fill-epsilon-x.md new -- a day-only name, which must never fold, since a resolver needs the whole stamp to compute a home
file tools/fixtures/session_logs_archive/README.md the fixture index names all five shapes and what each proves
file construction/REDS.md books %180 and %181, and the headline recounts to 181 rows
recommend keep-going the session-logs index stands at 2,895,041 bytes against the 24,576 its own header declares, because the living-pin roster never listed it -- the fold, the head repair, and a guard that reads a bound from the document rather than from a roster
